<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenian bank Vipa sees steady 1996 pretax.</title>
<headline>Slovenian bank Vipa sees steady 1996 pretax.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenia's listed bank Vipa on Monday said it expected 1996 pre-tax profit to hit 300 million tolars ($2.03 million), barely changed from the previous year.</p>
<p>&quot;Our balance sheet assets rose more than a quarter to 36 billion tolars, mostly because of increase of new clients,&quot; general manager Egidij Birsa told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said the bank's balance sheet is expected to rise by another 20 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Novica Mihajlovic, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
